// Title: Uninstall Crowdstrike Falcon Sensor
// Sigma ID: f0f7be61-9cf5-43be-9836-99d6ef448a18
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2021-07-12 | Modified: 2023-03-09
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Adversaries may disable security tools to avoid possible detection of their tools and activities
//   by uninstalling Crowdstrike Falcon
// False positives:
//   - Administrator might leverage the same command line for debugging or other purposes. However this action must be always investigated
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1562.001/T1562.001.md
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_uninstall_crowdstrike_falcon.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "\\WindowsSensor.exe" and ProcessCommandLine contains " /uninstall" and ProcessCommandLine contains " /quiet"
